<title>UK: John Lewis of Hungerford sets debut premium.</title>
<headline>John Lewis of Hungerford sets debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in John Lewis of Hungerford Plc, a kitchen maker, set a 25 percent premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Monday.</p>
<p>By 1045 GMT the shares were marked up at 3-3/4p, ahead of their issue price of 3p, although no trade was registered in the stock. The issue, which valued the company at 4.15 million stg, raised 1.15 million stg before expenses.</p>
<p>The broker to the float was Ellis &amp; Partners.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
